My approach to rings is to put them on once altarized, and if they have no
obvious effect, take them off again right away.  This does carry a remote
risk of polying on that one turn, or of getting clobbered if it's conflict
and something powerful is nearby, but it also immediately identifies
several useful rings.

> Better add headgear into the stuff you don't want to
> try on without IDing it. A couple are nasty, and one
> is an instant game loser IIUC.

The one you're thinking of, if it's the one I think you're thinking of,
doesn't immediately lose the game; but it can have serious and lasting
consequences.

